{"step_index":74,"source":"MODEL","type":"VIEW_FILE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T03:00:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-28T10:00:31+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-28T10:00:33+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/Makefile`\nTotal Lines: 197\nTotal Bytes: 9855\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # ── Cross-platform shell ──\n2: # Recipe trong file nay dung cu phap POSIX sh (while/read, pipeline, python heredoc). Chay\n3: # `make` tu PowerShell/cmd tren Windows thi make khong tim duoc sh nao va fail voi\n4: # \"The system cannot find the path specified. / Error 255\" - nen phai ghim ve Git Bash.\n5: #\n6: # TUYET DOI khong de make tu do `bash` tren PATH: may co WSL thi\n7: # C:\\Windows\\System32\\bash.exe duoc tim thay TRUOC Git Bash, va recipe se chay trong WSL -\n8: # noi `git`/`python3` la binary Linux va D:\\repo\\... khong ton tai.\n9: #\n10: # Dung ProgramW6432 chu KHONG dung ProgramFiles: make.exe (ezwinports/winget) la 32-bit nen\n11: # $(ProgramFiles) tra ve \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\" trong khi Git cai o \"C:\\Program Files\".\n12: # Sai duong dan thi make LANG LE bo qua SHELL vua gan va quay ve sh.exe/cmd.\n13: ifeq ($(OS),Windows_NT)\n14: PROGFILES := $(if $(ProgramW6432),$(ProgramW6432),$(ProgramFiles))\n15: GIT_ROOT  := $(subst \\,/,$(PROGFILES))/Git\n16: GIT_BASH  ?= $(GIT_ROOT)/usr/bin/bash.exe\n17: SHELL     := $(GIT_BASH)\n18: .SHELLFLAGS := -c\n19: # Git Bash chay tu PowerShell chi thua ke PATH cua Windows, KHONG co /usr/bin cua no\n20: # => grep/awk/python3 deu \"command not found\". Phai tu chen vao.\n21: export PATH := $(GIT_ROOT)/usr/bin;$(GIT_ROOT)/mingw64/bin;$(PATH)\n22: PWSH      := powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File\n23: else\n24: PWSH      := pwsh -NoProfile -File\n25: endif\n26: \n27: ROOT_DIR := $(abspath $(CURDIR)/../../../..)\n28: PROJECTS_JSON := $(ROOT_DIR)/.meta/00_projects.json\n29: PROJECT_INFO_JSON := $(CURDIR)/01_origin/project_info\n<truncated 1935 bytes>\ng lại (url, branch, thời điểm pull) vào 01_origin/project_info.json.\n69: # SAU KHI PULL PHẢI `make config` lại: appSetting.config/Web.config (và .pristine) bị xoá theo.\n70: #   make pull_code\n71: # sha cua ban clone tam duoc lay TRUOC khi xoa .git, roi ghi vao project_info.json\n72: # (bitbucket_commit) de truy nguoc snapshot ung voi commit nao cua repo goc.\n73: # Dung cp -a chu KHONG dung rsync: Git Bash tren Windows khong co rsync.\n74: pull_code:\n75: \t@python3 -c \"\\\n76: import json; \\\n77: d = json.load(open('$(PROJECTS_JSON)')); \\\n78: g = [g for g in d['root']['01_origin'] if g['name'] == '$(GROUP)'][0]; \\\n79: p = [p for p in g['projects'] if p['name'] == '$(APP)'][0]; \\\n80: print(p['bitbucket_url'] + '\\t' + p['bitbucket_branch']) \\\n81: \" | tr -d '\\r' | while IFS=$$'\\t' read -r url branch; do \\\n82: \t\tdest=\"$(CURDIR)/01_origin\"; \\\n83: \t\techo \"  Pull $$url @ $$branch -> $$dest\"; \\\n84: \t\ttmp=$$(mktemp -d); \\\n85: \t\tif git clone --quiet --filter=blob:none --depth 1 --single-branch --branch \"$$branch\" \"$$url\" \"$$tmp\"; then \\\n86: \t\t\tsha=$$(git -C \"$$tmp\" rev-parse HEAD); \\\n87: \t\t\trm -rf \"$$tmp/.git\" \"$$tmp/.gitmodules\"; \\\n88: \t\t\trm -rf \"$$dest\"; \\\n89: \t\t\tmkdir -p \"$$dest\"; \\\n90: \t\t\tcp -a \"$$tmp\"/. \"$$dest\"/; \\\n91: \t\t\trm -rf \"$$dest/.git\" \"$$dest/.gitmodules\"; \\\n92: \t\t\techo \"    OK [pulled $$url -> $$dest]\"; \\\n93: \t\t\tpython3 -c \"\\\n94: import json, os, datetime; \\\n95: path = '$(PROJECT_INFO_JSON)'; \\\n96: data = json.load(open(path)) if os.path.exists(path) and os.path.getsize(path) > 0 else {'group': '$(GROUP)', 'projects': {}}; \\\n97: data.setdefault('projects', {})['$(APP)'] = {'bitbucket_url': '$$url', 'bitbucket_branch': '$$branch', 'bitbucket_commit': '$$sha', 'last_pulled': datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat()}; \\\n98: json.dump(data, open(path, 'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False); \\\n99: \"; \\\n100: \t\telse \\\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
