{"step_index":226,"source":"MODEL","type":"VIEW_FILE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T07:11:43Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-28T14:11:43+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-28T14:11:44+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/tests/scripts/run-tests.sh`\nTotal Lines: 179\nTotal Bytes: 7483\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # Runs the four test tracks of store-location-web and writes tests/reports/test-report-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.md\n3: # from the real `dotnet test` output.\n4: #\n5: #   Unit        - no network (Moq over IApiHelper, compat converters, session store, auth filter)\n6: #   Integration - real ids1-uat Keycloak + MDM Permissions/ReadClient over HTTP\n7: #   Functional  - real host: every [MvcAuthorize] action anonymously + SSO-backed contracts\n8: #   Smoke       - real host + SSO session: every page / read-only Ajax endpoint answers 200\n9: #\n10: # Every track is BUILT first (Functional references the web project, and building it while the host runs\n11: # would hit locked DLLs), then Unit + Integration run, then the web host starts on $PLACE_WEB_PORT\n12: # (default 4784 = port of the registered Keycloak redirect_uri) for Functional + Smoke and is stopped after.\n13: # SSO credentials: PLACE_WEB_SSO_USERNAME / PLACE_WEB_SSO_PASSWORD or tests/.env (see tests/.env.example).\n14: set -u\n15: \n16: SCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n17: TESTS_DIR=\"$(cd \"$SCRIPT_DIR/..\" && pwd)\"\n18: APP_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$TESTS_DIR/..\" && pwd)\"\n19: WEB_DIR=\"$APP_ROOT/02_target/CoC.Web.Place\"\n20: REPORTS_DIR=\"$TESTS_DIR/reports\"\n21: PORT=\"${PLACE_WEB_PORT:-4784}\"\n22: export PLACE_WEB_BASE_URL=\"${PLACE_WEB_BASE_URL:-http://localhost:$PORT}\"\n23: \n24: # Functional/Smoke/Integration assert the UAT contract (ids1-uat, client place-uat.concung.vn, localhost:4784).\n25: # app.config at the app root is STAGING by workspace convention (port 5305, ids1-stg); stop early wi\n<truncated 1737 bytes>\n1: build_track() {\n62:   local track=\"$1\" out=\"$WORK/$1.build.txt\"\n63:   echo \"[$track] dotnet build\"\n64:   dotnet build \"$(project_of \"$track\")\" -nologo > \"$out\" 2>&1\n65:   local rc=$?\n66:   set_result \"$track\" warnings \"$(grep -E '^[[:space:]]*[0-9]+ Warning\\(s\\)' \"$out\" | tail -1 | grep -oE '[0-9]+' | head -1)\"\n67:   if [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\n68:     set_result \"$track\" buildfail \"$(grep -E ': error ' \"$out\" | sed -E 's/^[[:space:]]+//' | sort -u | head -10)\"\n69:   fi\n70:   return $rc\n71: }\n72: \n73: test_track() {\n74:   local track=\"$1\" out=\"$WORK/$1.test.txt\"\n75:   if [ -f \"$WORK/$track.buildfail\" ]; then\n76:     echo \"[$track] skipped: build failed\"\n77:     return 1\n78:   fi\n79:   echo \"[$track] dotnet test\"\n80:   dotnet test \"$(project_of \"$track\")\" --no-build -nologo --verbosity minimal > \"$out\" 2>&1\n81:   local rc=$?\n82:   local line\n83:   line=$(grep -E '(Passed|Failed)![[:space:]]+-[[:space:]]+Failed:' \"$out\" | tail -1)\n84:   if [ -n \"$line\" ]; then\n85:     set_result \"$track\" failed \"$(echo \"$line\" | sed -E 's/.*Failed:[[:space:]]*([0-9]+).*/\\1/')\"\n86:     set_result \"$track\" passed \"$(echo \"$line\" | sed -E 's/.*Passed:[[:space:]]*([0-9]+).*/\\1/')\"\n87:     set_result \"$track\" skipped \"$(echo \"$line\" | sed -E 's/.*Skipped:[[:space:]]*([0-9]+).*/\\1/')\"\n88:     set_result \"$track\" total \"$(echo \"$line\" | sed -E 's/.*Total:[[:space:]]*([0-9]+).*/\\1/')\"\n89:     set_result \"$track\" duration \"$(echo \"$line\" | sed -E 's/.*Duration:[[:space:]]*([^-]+) -.*/\\1/' | sed -E 's/[[:space:]]+$//')\"\n90:   fi\n91:   grep -E '^[[:space:]]+Failed [^ ]' \"$out\" | sed -E 's/^[[:space:]]+Failed /- [FAIL] /; s/ \\[[^]]*\\]$//' > \"$WORK/$track.fails\"\n92:   tail -n 3 \"$out\"\n93:   return $rc\n94: }\n95: \n96: OVERALL=0\n97: for t in $TRACKS; do build_track \"$t\" || OVERALL=1; done\n98: \n99: test_track Unit || OVERALL=1\n100: test_track Integration || OVERALL=1\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
