{"step_index":896,"source":"MODEL","type":"VIEW_FILE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:12:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-29T16:12:29+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-29T16:12:29+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/02_target/CoC.Web.Place/Permission/UserPrincipal.cs`\nTotal Lines: 263\nTotal Bytes: 11600\nShowing lines 80 to 110\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n80: \r\n81:         /// <summary>Session-only overlay of the [JsonIgnore] secrets kept by UserSessionStore under its second key.</summary>\r\n82:         public void RestoreTokens(string token, string refreshToken, List<int> roleIDs)\r\n83:         {\r\n84:             _Token = token;\r\n85:             _refreshToken = refreshToken;\r\n86:             _roleIDs = roleIDs;\r\n87:         }\r\n88:         //AI[MIGRATE_END]\r\n89: \r\n90:         private List<PermissionRes> _userPermission;\r\n91:         public List<PermissionRes> UserPermission\r\n92:         {\r\n93:             get\r\n94:             {\r\n95:                 if (_userPermission == null) _userPermission = GetUserPermission();\r\n96:                 return _userPermission;\r\n97:             }\r\n98:         }\r\n99: \r\n100:         private List<ModuleRes> _module;\r\n101:         public List<ModuleRes> Module\r\n102:         {\r\n103:             get\r\n104:             {\r\n105:                 if (_module == null) _module = GetUserModule();\r\n106:                 return _module;\r\n107:             }\r\n108:         }\r\n109: \r\n110:         private int _positionID { get; set; }\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":897,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:12:29Z","thinking":"Analyzing the `UserPrincipal.cs` code, specifically the `RestoreTokens` method, which appears to manage session token restoration. This method updates internal token, refresh token, and role ID fields, clearing the `_userPermission` and `_module` properties. This suggests a potential session-related token refresh mechanism.\n\n\nThe getters for `UserPermission` and `Module` use lazy loading, checking if the corresponding backing field is null and `_roleIDs` is not null before populating them. Initialization outside of the constructor or deserialization might bypass this check. When `RestoreTokens` is invoked, `_userPermission` and `_module` are reset. The code correctly handles the case where `_roleIDs` is empty, as it will result in fetching an empty list, which represents a user with no roles. A potential race condition exists if the `Permission.Data` is null when `GetUserPermission()` is called, as the permissions could be loaded later.\n\n\nThe current implementation may cache an empty permission list if `Permission.Data` is null initially. This could lead to stale data even after the permission data is loaded. Ensuring `_userPermission` is only populated when `Permission.HasPermissionData` is true should fix this. The proposed change to the `UserPermission` getter will enforce this check, ensuring that an empty list is only cached if the data is actually available and no roles exist.\n\n\nThe getter for `UserPermission` and `Module` now correctly implements lazy loading with an additional check for `Permission.HasPermissionData`. This ensures that an empty list isn't cached if permission data isn't available, preventing stale data issues. The code's structure elegantly handles this case by only caching the data when it's available. `RestoreTokens` now resets the user permissions and modules, and this logic correctly utilizes the lazy loading behavior.\n\n\nThe constructor initializes `_roleIDs` from claims and the getters for `_userPermission` and `_module` use lazy loading, checking for `_roleIDs`. Session serialization captures populated `_userPermission` during the save operation. During deserialization, `_roleIDs` is `null`, and the getter for `_userPermission` will return an empty list because the lazy loading check returns an empty list, and the backing field will not be set.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"dotnet test tests/Unit/CoC.Web.Place.Unit.Tests\"","Cwd":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-store-location-web\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Running Unit Tests\"","toolSummary":"\"Run Unit Tests\""}}]}
