{"step_index":910,"source":"MODEL","type":"VIEW_FILE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:13:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-29T16:13:25+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-29T16:13:25+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/tests/scripts/run-tests.sh`\nTotal Lines: 180\nTotal Bytes: 7547\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # Runs the four test tracks of store-location-web and writes tests/reports/test-report-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.md\n3: # from the real `dotnet test` output.\n4: #\n5: #   Unit        - no network (Moq over IApiHelper, compat converters, session store, auth filter)\n6: #   Integration - real ids1-uat Keycloak + MDM Permissions/ReadClient over HTTP\n7: #   Functional  - real host: every [MvcAuthorize] action anonymously + SSO-backed contracts\n8: #   Smoke       - real host + SSO session: every page / read-only Ajax endpoint answers 200\n9: #\n10: # Every track is BUILT first (Functional references the web project, and building it while the host runs\n11: # would hit locked DLLs), then Unit + Integration run, then the web host starts on $PLACE_WEB_PORT\n12: # (default 4784 = port of the registered Keycloak redirect_uri) for Functional + Smoke and is stopped after.\n13: # SSO credentials: PLACE_WEB_SSO_USERNAME / PLACE_WEB_SSO_PASSWORD or tests/.env (see tests/.env.example).\n14: set -u\n15: export PATH=\"/usr/bin:/bin:$PATH\"\n16: \n17: SCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n18: TESTS_DIR=\"$(cd \"$SCRIPT_DIR/..\" && pwd)\"\n19: APP_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$TESTS_DIR/..\" && pwd)\"\n20: WEB_DIR=\"$APP_ROOT/02_target/CoC.Web.Place\"\n21: REPORTS_DIR=\"$TESTS_DIR/reports\"\n22: PORT=\"${PLACE_WEB_PORT:-4784}\"\n23: export PLACE_WEB_BASE_URL=\"${PLACE_WEB_BASE_URL:-http://localhost:$PORT}\"\n24: \n25: # Functional/Smoke/Integration assert the UAT contract (ids1-uat, client place-uat.concung.vn, localhost:4784).\n26: # app.config at the app root is STAGING by workspace convention (port 5305, ids1-stg); stop early with the fix\n27: # instead of letting 300+ tests fail on a redirect_uri/port mismatch.\n28: APPSETTINGS=\"$WEB_DIR/appsettings.json\"\n29: CLIENT_URL=$(grep -oE '\"ClientUrl\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"[^\"]*\"' \"$APPSETTINGS\" 2>/dev/null | head -1 | sed -E 's/.*\"([^\"]*)\"$/\\1/')\n30: if [ \"$CLIENT_URL\" != \"http://localhost:$PORT/\" ] || ! grep -q 'ids1-uat.concung.vn' \"$APPSETTINGS\"; then\n31:   echo \"LOI: target appsettings.json dang o moi truong khac UAT (ClientUrl=${CLIENT_URL:-?}).\"\n32:   echo \"     Test suite nay kiem hop dong UAT (ids1-uat, localhost:$PORT). Chay truoc:\"\n33:   echo \"       make -C \\\"$APP_ROOT\\\" config ENV=uat\"\n34:   echo \"     xong test thi 'make config' de may ve lai staging.\"\n35:   exit 2\n36: fi\n37: \n38: mkdir -p \"$REPORTS_DIR\"\n39: TIMESTAMP=$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)\n40: REPORT=\"$REPORTS_DIR/test-report-$TIMESTAMP.md\"\n41: WORK=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n42: HOST_LOG=\"$WORK/host.log\"\n43: SDK_VERSION=$(dotnet --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)\n44: TRACKS=\"Unit Integration Functional Smoke\"\n45: \n46: kill_port() {\n47:   if [ \"${OS:-}\" = \"Windows_NT\" ]; then\n48:     for p in $(netstat -ano | grep -i LISTENING | awk -v port=\":$PORT\" '$2 ~ port\"$\" {print $5}' | sort -u | grep -vE '^(0|4)$'); do\n49:       MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 taskkill /F /PID \"$p\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n50:     done\n51:   else\n52:     for p in $(lsof -ti:\"$PORT\" -sTCP:LISTEN 2>/dev/null); do kill -9 \"$p\" 2>/dev/null || true; done\n53:   fi\n54: }\n55: \n56: project_of() { echo \"$TESTS_DIR/$1/CoC.Web.Place.$1.Tests/CoC.Web.Place.$1.Tests.csproj\"; }\n57: \n58: # per-track results live in files so plain POSIX-ish bash (no associative arrays) is enough\n59: set_result() { echo \"$3\" > \"$WORK/$1.$2\"; }\n60: get_result() { cat \"$WORK/$1.$2\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"$3\"; }\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":911,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:13:25Z","thinking":"The configuration setting influences authorization behavior. Specifically, the \"UAT\" environment bypasses authorization checks, while \"STG\" enforces them. A discrepancy exists where a permission check is bypassed in the UAT environment, potentially explaining observed behavior in the \"ValidStaffSession\" test. This difference suggests that the environment configuration impacts the execution path, notably impacting permission enforcement within the test.\n\n\nIn \"STAGING\", the permission data being null led to an empty `UserPermission` list, triggering a 403 error during authorization. The `IsAuthorize` method checks for null permissions and environment, returning false if null and true for certain environments. The `UserPrincipal` class's `RestoreTokens` method sets the permission to null, which is used to initialize the `UserPermission` list if it is not already set.\n\n\nDuring session deserialization, the role IDs are lost, leading to incorrect permission initialization because the deserialized object's `UserPermission` method evaluates a different conditional path. The `RestoreTokens` method later restores the role IDs, but doesn't correctly reinitialize the `UserPermission` field, leaving it null. This means the object is in an inconsistent state after loading from the session. Subsequently, accessing `UserPermission` in an authorization context causes a recalculation of permissions based on the restored role IDs, which is the intended behavior, yet it is happening later.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":"false","MatchPerLine":"true","Query":"\"PrincipalKey\"","SearchPath":"\"e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web\"","toolAction":"\"Searching for PrincipalKey\"","toolSummary":"\"Search PrincipalKey\""}}]}
