{"step_index":1225,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:37:24Z","thinking":"The test `Json_WritesNewtonsoftPascalCase_LikeCoreMvcJsonNetResult` confirms a codebase-wide adherence to Newtonsoft PascalCase for JSON serialization, mirroring `Core.MVC`'s behavior. The focus now shifts to `APIClient` to verify it conforms to this standard.\n\n```\n\n\nThe porting of the `APIClient` likely introduced serialization issues due to the use of `PostAsJsonAsync` with an `object` argument. When the argument is of type `object`, the serializer will generate an empty JSON object, `{}`. This is because the type `object` has no properties to serialize. Additionally, `System.Net.Http.Json` uses `System.Text.Json` with camelCase naming by default, which introduces an incompatibility with assumed PascalCase naming.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"pwsh -Command \\\"try { Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'https://place-api-stg4.concung.vn/api/Scopes/GetListMVC' -Method POST -Body '{}' -ContentType 'application/json' } catch { $_.Exception.Response.StatusCode.value__; $_.ErrorDetails.Message; $_.Exception.Message }\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing Scopes/GetListMVC with empty json\"","toolSummary":"\"Test Scopes/GetListMVC with empty json\""}}]}
