{"step_index":1768,"source":"MODEL","type":"VIEW_FILE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T10:44:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-29T17:44:30+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-29T17:44:30+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/02_target/Makefile`\nTotal Lines: 130\nTotal Bytes: 6292\nShowing lines 1 to 130\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #AI[MIGRATE_START]: Phase 0C bat buoc - harness chay/verify local cho ban port .NET 10 (OLD chi chay duoc trong Visual Studio + IIS Express); mau lay tu skill fe-migration templates/Makefile + phan Windows/Git Bash cua hrm-web da chay that\n2: # Makefile for CoC.Web.Place (store-location-web) post-migration (MVC5+AngularJS -> .NET 10, keep-structure)\n3: # Usage: make <target>\n4: #\n5: #   - No Swagger endpoint -> HEALTH_PATH targets a plain controller route\n6: #   - Accepts 200/301/302 (redirect-to-login = healthy, not a failure)\n7: #   - Verify log/pid derived from PROJECT_DIR+PORT to avoid collision with API verify\n8: #   - `test` target: xunit project in tests/\n9: #\n10: # --no-launch-profile is REQUIRED on every `dotnet run` below: `dotnet run` reads\n11: # launchSettings.json's own `applicationUrl` and silently overrides ASPNETCORE_URLS.\n12: # It also drops ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development, so that is exported explicitly.\n13: \n14: .PHONY: help kill-port build run clean restore watch start dev verify test\n15: \n16: # ---- Cross-platform shell -------------------------------------------------------\n17: # Recipes use POSIX sh syntax. On Windows pin Git Bash explicitly: `bash` on PATH may be\n18: # WSL (C:\\Windows\\System32\\bash.exe) where `dotnet` and D:\\ paths do not exist.\n19: # Git installed elsewhere? Override: make build GIT_BASH=D:/Git/usr/bin/bash.exe\n20: ifeq ($(OS),Windows_NT)\n21: # ProgramW6432 (not ProgramFiles): a 32-bit make.exe sees \"Program Files (x86)\".\n22: PROGFILES := $(if $(ProgramW6432),$(ProgramW6432),$(ProgramFiles))\n23: GIT_ROOT  := $(s\n<truncated 3284 bytes>\n: kill-port\n88: \tdotnet build $(CSPROJ)\n89: \n90: run: kill-port\n91: \t@echo \"Starting $(PROJECT_DIR) on http://localhost:$(PORT)/ ...\"\n92: \tcd $(PROJECT_DIR) && ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://+:$(PORT) ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development dotnet run --no-launch-profile\n93: \n94: watch: kill-port\n95: \tcd $(PROJECT_DIR) && ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://+:$(PORT) ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development dotnet watch run --no-launch-profile\n96: \n97: clean:\n98: \tdotnet clean $(CSPROJ)\n99: \n100: start: kill-port build run\n101: \n102: dev: kill-port restore build run\n103: \n104: # Verify: build, run in the BACKGROUND, hit HEALTH_PATH, report pass/fail, then stop.\n105: # 200/301/302 all count as healthy (unauthenticated MVC routes redirect to /accounts/login).\n106: verify: kill-port build\n107: \t@echo \"Starting $(PROJECT_DIR) in background for verification (port $(PORT))...\"\n108: \t@cd $(PROJECT_DIR) && ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://+:$(PORT) ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development nohup dotnet run --no-launch-profile --no-build > $(VERIFY_LOG) 2>&1 & echo $$! > $(VERIFY_PID)\n109: \t@ATTEMPTS=0; \\\n110: \tuntil curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" http://localhost:$(PORT)$(HEALTH_PATH) 2>/dev/null | grep -q \"200\\|301\\|302\"; do \\\n111: \t\tATTEMPTS=$$((ATTEMPTS+1)); \\\n112: \t\tif [ $$ATTEMPTS -ge 60 ]; then \\\n113: \t\t\techo \"FAILED: app did not respond on port $(PORT) within 60s.\"; \\\n114: \t\t\ttail -n 50 $(VERIFY_LOG) 2>/dev/null || true; \\\n115: \t\t\tkill -9 $$(cat $(VERIFY_PID)) 2>/dev/null || true; $(KILL_BY_PORT); \\\n116: \t\t\trm -f $(VERIFY_PID); \\\n117: \t\t\texit 1; \\\n118: \t\tfi; \\\n119: \t\tsleep 1; \\\n120: \tdone; \\\n121: \tSTATUS=$$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" http://localhost:$(PORT)$(HEALTH_PATH)); \\\n122: \techo \"VERIFY PASSED: $(HEALTH_PATH) responded with HTTP $$STATUS\"\n123: \t@kill -9 $$(cat $(VERIFY_PID)) 2>/dev/null || true\n124: \t@$(KILL_BY_PORT)\n125: \t@rm -f $(VERIFY_PID) $(VERIFY_LOG)\n126: \n127: test:\n128: \t@$(TEST_BASH) $(TEST_DIR)/scripts/run-tests.sh\n129: #AI[MIGRATE_END]\n130: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
