{"step_index":2443,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T03:14:32Z","thinking":"Initial suspicion centers on the use of `JsonContent` and how it interacts with the HTTP client's POST operation. Investigation aims to clarify the behavior of `JsonContent`, specifically whether it pre-computes the content length. This step is critical to understanding the data transfer process.\n\n\n`JsonContent` likely streams its content, potentially leading to chunked transfer encoding if the content length isn't predetermined. This could cause issues with older WebApi 2 endpoints or handlers like compression or logging, if they are expecting a `Content-Length`. Conversely, `StringContent` pre-computes the length, which guarantees a `Content-Length`. The critical difference hinges on how `JsonContent` streams the content during serialization.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Net.Http\\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Net.Http.Json\\n\\n$t = [string]\\n$jc = [System.Net.Http.Json.JsonContent]::Create(\\\"hello\\\", [string], $null, $null)\\nWrite-Host \\\"Before buffering:\\\"\\nWrite-Host \\\"  Content-Length: $($jc.Headers.ContentLength)\\\"\\nWrite-Host \\\"  Transfer-Encoding chunked: $($null -eq $jc.Headers.ContentLength)\\\"\\n\\n$jc.LoadIntoBufferAsync().Wait()\\nWrite-Host \\\"After buffering:\\\"\\nWrite-Host \\\"  Content-Length: $($jc.Headers.ContentLength)\\\"\\n\"","Description":"\"Check JsonContent Content-Length before and after buffering\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\25303_TruongVanTinh\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity-ide\\\\brain\\\\3fcfde30-4110-403c-8f9f-a4ed95abc9e6\\\\scratch\\\\check_chunked.ps1\"","toolAction":"\"Write chunked test script\"","toolSummary":"\"Check if JsonContent lacks Content-Length\""}}]}
