{"step_index":2584,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T03:44:10Z","thinking":"The task involves addressing a bug identified by the tag `TC-FUNC-003-fix-apiclient-pascalcase-serialization`. Observing existing fix tags, the goal is to follow a defined bug-fixing process. `DEV_HANDBOOK.md` provides guidance, specifically indicating that fixes should be developed on a `fix/*` branch and merged directly.\n\n\nFirst, the running terminal needs to be checked to see if it can be safely stopped, since the API call appears successful. Following the documented process, the `appsettings.json` file requires reverting the `ClientUrl` setting to the staging environment address. Next, a bug report dossier must be created, following the format in the appendix of the handbook.\n\n\nSerialization issues stem from object serialization being empty, exacerbated by inconsistent casing and chunked encoding. System.Text.Json (STJ) combined with a null `PropertyNamingPolicy` and `StringContent` offers a fix. Successful test runs with 72/72 tests passing and local verification confirm the solution. A fix branch is created, commits are staged, and then merged back into the `dev` branch.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"git status\"","Cwd":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-store-location-web\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking git status\"","toolSummary":"\"Check git status\""}}]}
