{"step_index":3013,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T08:02:22Z","thinking":"The `wwwroot` directory contains 374 files. A case-insensitive dictionary will pre-index these files at startup, mapping relative paths to their correctly-cased counterparts on disk. This pre-indexing approach aims to streamline and expedite file lookups during HTTP request handling.\n\n\nA dictionary lookup with pre-indexed paths ensures fast, case-insensitive file resolution, rewriting requests to the correct case before disk access. This lookup takes minimal memory and negligible time. Further investigation reveals a potential issue with AngularJS directives where the `src` attribute could lead to premature requests before compilation; `ng-src` should prevent these.\n\n\nThe `_Layout.cshtml` file appears to load `your_style.css` twice, and also mixes the correct and incorrect directory casing. Correcting these redundancies and casing inconsistencies in the file would streamline the loading process. According to the document, creating a pull request is unnecessary; the standard flow involves merging directly into the `dev` branch after committing the fix on a dedicated `fix/*` branch.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"git status\"","Cwd":"\"e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"2000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"git status\""}}]}
