AngularJS trong [_ModalRoutePlace.cshtml](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/02_target/CoC.Web.Place/Views/Home/_ModalRoutePlace.cshtml)**:\n     * Đổi `src=\"{{item2.URL_Thumbnai}}\"` thành `ng-src=\"{{item2.URL_Thumbnai}}\"` để tránh trình duyệt bắn request 404 trước khi Angular render.\n  3. **Chuẩn hóa link stylesheet trong [_Layout.cshtml](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/02_target/CoC.Web.Place/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml)**:\n     * Xóa dòng duplicate `your_style.css`, chuẩn hóa đường dẫn, bảo toàn UTF-8 BOM.\n  4. **Tạo hồ sơ bug** trong `04_critical_change/test-report-20260930-141547/`.\n  5. **Thực hiện merge `dev`, gắn tag và merge `staging10`, `staging`** theo đúng Handbook.\n\nTôi bắt đầu thực hiện ngay nhé?","thinking":"Examining existing dossiers to establish context for the next bug code, `TC-FUNC-004-case-insensitive-static-files-linux`. The file is located within a specific directory related to a critical change and test report. The focus will be on the cause of case-insensitive behavior in static file handling on Linux.\n\n\nAccording to the documentation, pull requests are not required for this type of fix within the migration project; direct merging into the `dev` branch is the standard procedure for bug fixes.  The established process involves creating a `fix/*` branch, making the code changes and creating associated documentation, committing, merging into `dev` directly, pushing to the remote repository, tagging the commit with the fix identifier, and then merging from `dev` to `staging10` and `staging`. This triggers automated deployment.\n\n\n"}
