{"step_index":3802,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T08:26:49Z","thinking":"The connection error from DBeaver indicates a problem with the \"TimeZone\" parameter, specifically with the \"Asia/Saigon\" value. Reviewing the Python script, `sslmode=\"require\"` was also present, raising a concern if the database server requires a different timezone setting or if SSL is incorrectly configured. The DBeaver error suggests the timezone is the immediate point of failure, although the SSL configuration could still be a contributing factor.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"\\\"invalid value for parameter \\\\\\\"TimeZone\\\\\\\"\\\" \\\"DBeaver\\\" postgresql\"","toolAction":"\"Searching for DBeaver PostgreSQL timezone fix\"","toolSummary":"\"Search DBeaver timezone error fix\""}}]}
{"step_index":3803,"source":"MODEL","type":"SEARCH_WEB","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T08:26:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-01T15:26:57+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-01T15:27:04+07:00\nThe search for \"\"invalid value for parameter \\\"TimeZone\\\"\" \"DBeaver\" postgresql\" returned the following summary:\nThis error typically occurs because your local system (or the environment running DBeaver) is using a timezone name (e.g., `Asia/Calcutta` or `Asia/Saigon`) that the PostgreSQL server version you are connecting to does not recognize as a valid or current timezone identifier[1][2][3].\n\nHere are the most effective ways to resolve this:\n\n### Method 1: Enable \"Replace Legacy Time Zone\" in DBeaver\nThis is often the quickest fix within the DBeaver application itself[4].\n1.  Open DBeaver and right-click your PostgreSQL connection in the **Database Navigator**.\n2.  Select **Edit Connection**.\n3.  Go to **Connection settings** > **Advanced** > **Settings** (or look for the **Driver properties** tab).\n4.  Look for an option labeled **\"Replace legacy time zone\"** and ensure it is checked/enabled[4].\n5.  Save and test your connection.\n\n### Method 2: Modify `dbeaver.ini` (JVM Timezone)\nIf the above does not work, you can force DBeaver to use a compatible timezone (such as `UTC` or a newer standard name like `Asia/Kolkata` instead of the deprecated `Asia/Calcutta`) by editing the configuration file[5].\n1.  Navigate to your DBeaver installation folder (e.g., `C:\\Users\\<YourUser>\\AppData\\Local\\DBeaver` on Windows)[5].\n2.  Open the `dbeaver.ini` file in a text editor[5].\n3.  Find the `-vmargs` line[5].\n4.  Immediately after `-vmargs`, add the following line[5]:\n    `-Duser.timezone=UTC`\n    *(Alternatively, use a known valid timezone like `Asia/Kolkata` if you must keep the local time offset[5].)*\n5.  Save the file and **restart DBeaver**[5].\n\n### Why this happens\n*   **Deprecated Timezone Names:** Some older timezone databases (or specific PostgreSQL configurations) no longer support historical names like `Asia/Calcutta`[1][6]. They expect modern counterparts like `Asia/Kolkata`[7][6].\n*   **JDBC Driver Behavior:** The PostgreSQL JDBC driver\n<truncated 558 bytes>\n1y9wTokJGK1NgTHyt6RlYwwv2WJ8bXTE-xvy_pi6mX_cFAoojJ0_eHTVC3I0YcfrkcIS21aV2OiQl5WNq4MD5IJPGo14A==)\n[2] [facebook.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHram32cEIONFdYATjV9FEnMu5DFZBQXtotp7DtWieMW-MBH9cfzNqwVcRijPl1vQHP45xmIQAWPkqebT2vLBHib3Pj8kvpYyqs22YS22PsZ41ZFeZVW059TZvbFvQQWeLeWbVlOy7hV2DKPxqXOyIhGEq3-4DgcUZSoy-T-g==)\n[3] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEOLv_pHHI-wc5PZxqM5mrBdJUGrGIkcH3OomLP91vCR9QfhVc7RWc1RIL63sbiGpz7utF2eccgVfLd4z0e36Z1_PFbEZR7ejJ3QaHnkmlxJWFl3ZonNUSQX0nN5mmbASWc)\n[4] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGL9RtNqW73B7xrgohRBOmdbDW6LT18f1DdzCBALvmEmnSQB2SJ1BeluU9cc-pMcsB9Z7nnSIC1EnA_x6DFNhFvKcOQI7oZJOAHg05PtpFAMxIJ0XOPoTRTmCUmnwxg8Fs10FQbcBB_hU-S-TeXkXaDwZLk4fGrvBsID3YmmYUN5cYo2ikofL0GNkTskr3k3U2zBPnASxWL4_bdZpT8hgrTsHrDJuDsYJeqGNdUDFxXaQ==)\n[5] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF4_zcoH_pKA4MAJvPIGGm8fRjewUrlu9fQYs7JXsj4OnVueGuyV6dHN9N0wZFwODNKGCMd67SdkFxuG3iMBd83Mg0gBiEeBFr_tt4MdKZ6TtyJxoy41OhBr-ZgureJCOeND_HVQiFEJeC1PWNMu6Z--Ja7mPpRVR1zHwB9ix05cOSJK0SsZLT2XbJCGoijfzuab7LJK48=)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGL9RtNqW73B7xrgohRBOmdbDW6LT18f1DdzCBALvmEmnSQB2SJ1BeluU9cc-pMcsB9Z7nnSIC1EnA_x6DFNhFvKcOQI7oZJOAHg05PtpFAMxIJ0XOPoTRTmCUmnwxg8Fs10FQbcBB_hU-S-TeXkXaDwZLk4fGrvBsID3YmmYUN5cYo2ikofL0GNkTskr3k3U2zBPnASxWL4_bdZpT8hgrTsHrDJuDsYJeqGNdUDFxXaQ==)\n[7] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHB9n3j6P_sQzzml5pUIbVs7RjTieE3K-4-BAhVr6KSSUMvT5AsJR7sNfKbEDvWs0J-_4z1LKqXmMAFiyN5xkFlHdRcl4ClUI5hP1i6Ar8ORW1FIdS1QV0u55C86UC3_VFpdCkcKK7T