{"step_index":5331,"source":"MODEL","type":"VIEW_FILE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-06T08:56:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-06T15:56:38+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-06T15:56:39+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/tests/Functional/CoC.Web.SCM.Functional/JsonCompatibilityTests.cs`\nTotal Lines: 159\nTotal Bytes: 6241\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: using System.IO;\r\n2: using System.Net.Http;\r\n3: using System.Text;\r\n4: using System.Text.Json;\r\n5: using System.Threading.Tasks;\r\n6: using Xunit;\r\n7: \r\n8: namespace CoC.Web.SCM.Functional\r\n9: {\r\n10:     /// <summary>\r\n11:     /// Tests to verify JSON serialization uses PascalCase for AngularJS compatibility.\r\n12:     /// \r\n13:     /// Program.cs configures:\r\n14:     ///   .AddJsonOptions(o => o.JsonSerializerOptions.PropertyNamingPolicy = null)\r\n15:     /// \r\n16:     /// This means property names are NOT transformed to camelCase; they preserve\r\n17:     /// their original C# PascalCase naming (matching AngularJS frontend expectations).\r\n18:     /// \r\n19:     /// NOTE: Controller actions that return JSON require IApiHelper (not registered\r\n20:     /// in test DI), so HTTP-level JSON response tests are skipped. Serialization\r\n21:     /// behavior is verified directly via JsonSerializer.\r\n22:     /// </summary>\r\n23:     public class JsonCompatibilityTests : IClassFixture<AppFactory>\r\n24:     {\r\n25:         private readonly AppFactory _factory;\r\n26: \r\n27:         public JsonCompatibilityTests(AppFactory factory)\r\n28:         {\r\n29:             _factory = factory;\r\n30:         }\r\n31: \r\n32:         [Fact]\r\n33:         public void JsonSerializer_Default_PreservesPascalCase()\r\n34:         {\r\n35:             // Verify that JsonSerializerOptions with no naming policy preserves PascalCase\r\n36:             var options = new JsonSerializerOptions\r\n37:             {\r\n38:                 PropertyNamingPolicy = null // Same as \n<truncated 829 bytes>\nage\\\"\", json);\r\n56:         }\r\n57: \r\n58:         [Fact]\r\n59:         public void JsonSerializer_CamelCase_WouldTransformNames()\r\n60:         {\r\n61:             // Verify that camelCase naming policy WOULD transform names\r\n62:             // (confirming that our choice of null is intentional for PascalCase)\r\n63:             var camelOptions = new JsonSerializerOptions\r\n64:             {\r\n65:                 PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase\r\n66:             };\r\n67: \r\n68:             var obj = new { Status = \"Success\", Message = \"Test\" };\r\n69:             var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(obj, camelOptions);\r\n70: \r\n71:             Assert.Contains(\"status\", json);   // camelCase applied\r\n72:             Assert.Contains(\"message\", json);  // camelCase applied\r\n73:             Assert.DoesNotContain(\"Status\", json);\r\n74:             Assert.DoesNotContain(\"Message\", json);\r\n75:         }\r\n76: \r\n77:         [Fact]\r\n78:         public void JsonSerializer_MatchesProgramConfiguration()\r\n79:         {\r\n80:             // Replicate Program.cs configuration exactly\r\n81:             var options = new JsonSerializerOptions();\r\n82:             options.PropertyNamingPolicy = null; // Program.cs setting\r\n83: \r\n84:             var payload = new\r\n85:             {\r\n86:                 UserID = 1,\r\n87:                 Username = \"testuser\",\r\n88:                 FullName = \"Test User\",\r\n89:                 IsActive = true\r\n90:             };\r\n91: \r\n92:             var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(payload, options);\r\n93: \r\n94:             // All properties should retain their PascalCase names\r\n95:             Assert.Contains(\"\\\"UserID\\\"\", json);\r\n96:             Assert.Contains(\"\\\"Username\\\"\", json);\r\n97:             Assert.Contains(\"\\\"FullName\\\"\", json);\r\n98:             Assert.Contains(\"\\\"IsActive\\\"\", json);\r\n99:         }\r\n100: \r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
