not-found exception occurs, resulting in a Kubernetes `CrashLoopBackOff` status and a 503 Ingress error. The absence of this library is a likely cause of the recent deployment failures.\n\nInvestigating configuration differences begins by comparing the application's configuration files with staging environment settings. An unexpected staging URL configuration was found; this discrepancy requires further examination.\n\n\nThe observed error, `/OutputFastSaleReFunds` failure, is linked to a specific staging API URL. Further, `cci.core.json` and associated configurations are being investigated for discrepancies and potential clues.\n\nRedis configuration checks confirm a valid Redis server and credentials on the staging network. Kibana settings, as observed in `cci.core.json`, are also being reviewed for consistency.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$body = @{\\n    client_id     = \\\"scm.ClientCredential\\\"\\n    client_secret = \\\"6D9F85\\\"\\n    scope         = \\\"scm-api\\\"\\n    grant_type    = \\\"client_credentials\\\"\\n}\\ntry {\\n    $resp = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri \\\"https://ids1-stg.concung.vn/realms/master/protocol/openid-connect/token\\\" -Method Post -Body $body -ContentType \\\"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\\\"\\n    Write-Host \\\"Success getting token: $($resp.token_type) - $($resp.access_token.Substring(0, 30))...\\\"\\n} catch {\\n    Write-Host \\\"Failed: $($_.Exception.Message)\\\"\\n    if ($_.Exception.Response) {\\n        $reader = New-Object System.IO.StreamReader($_.Exception.Response.GetResponseStream())\\n        Write-Host $reader.ReadToEnd()\\n    }\\n}\"","Cwd":"\"E:\\\\Work\\\\dev-ops\\\\vaults-gitops\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Test Keycloak token for scm.ClientCredential\""}}]}
