{"step_index":6286,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T09:24:37Z","thinking":"The application is encountering a `PlatformNotSupportedException` related to `System.Drawing.Common`. The error occurs during the construction of an `ImageConverter` object. This suggests the code is using `System.Drawing.Common`, which is not supported on the current platform, likely due to a Windows-only platform restriction introduced in .NET 6 and later versions.\n\n\nThe exception arises during ASP.NET Core's route configuration because a public controller method, `ImageToByteArray`, has an `System.Drawing.Image` parameter. Routing scans controllers during startup and tries to create metadata for parameters, which leads to instantiation of the unsupported `ImageConverter` on Linux when the parameter type is `System.Drawing.Image`. The code causing this issue requires further investigation to determine why this method was added in the first place, or if it is now required.\n\n\nLine 85 in `Program.cs` indicates the error source; however, this file has been significantly refactored in the current development branch. The code causing the error likely exists in an older branch, or commit, which hasn't received the `[NonAction]` attribute on `ImageToByteArray`. The older version does not have the refactored code and lacks the `[NonAction]` attribute. This older code base is where the `MapControllerRoute` call, which triggers metadata creation, exists.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":"false","Includes":"[\"*BarcodePrintsController*.cs\"]","IsRegex":"false","MatchPerLine":"true","Query":"\"Image\"","SearchPath":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-scm-web\\\\02_target\\\\CoC.Web.SCM\"","toolAction":"\"Searching BarcodePrintsController for Image\"","toolSummary":"\"Search BarcodePrintsController Image\""}}]}
