{"step_index":6594,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:08Z","thinking":"A hardcoded path in a previous report comparison script necessitates a dedicated script for the current project. Initial thought was to replicate the existing file structure, but a review of available scripts revealed a JavaScript report generator. This suggests the need to create a new Python comparator script, `compare-parity.py`, that flexibly reads report data either from command-line arguments or defaults to the specified report directory.\n\n\nThe next step is to run the NET4 and NET10 test suites and compare the results. The existing command lines for running the tests are identified. Based on past runtimes, each suite will take about two hours.\n\nThe total parity check sequence will require approximately four hours. An orchestration script, `run-parity.win.ps1`, is planned to manage the execution and comparison.\n\n\nNow executing the E2E tests for both environments. The first test run targets the baseline environment. Upon completion, the second run will execute against the target. Each execution's duration is being captured for future analysis.\n\nA final comparison phase will use the Python script to analyze and report on parity between the two test runs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import json\\nimport glob\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\n\\nif sys.stdout.encoding != 'utf-8':\\n    try:\\n        sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n\\ndef find_latest_report(details_dir, prefix):\\n    files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(details_dir, f\\\"{prefix}-report-*.json\\\")))\\n    files = [f for f in files if not f.endswith(\\\"-latest.json\\\")]\\n    if not files:\\n        latest = os.path.join(details_dir, f\\\"{prefix}-report-latest.json\\\")\\n        if os.path.exists(latest):\\n            return latest\\n        return None\\n    return files[-1]\\n\\ndef extract_tests(report_path):\\n    with open(report_path, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n        data = json.load(f)\\n    tests = {}\\n    for screen in data.get(\\\"screens\\\", []):\\n        screen_name = screen.get(\\\"screen\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n        for t in screen.get(\\\"tests\\\", []):\\n            tc = t.get(\\\"tc\\\") or \\\"\\\"\\n            scenario = t.get(\\\"scenario\\\") or \\\"\\\"\\n            file_path = t.get(\\\"file\\\") or \\\"\\\"\\n            key = f\\\"{screen_name} | {tc} | {scenario}\\\"\\n            tests[key] = {\\n                \\\"screen\\\": screen_name,\\n                \\\"tc\\\": tc,\\n                \\\"scenario\\\": scenario,\\n                \\\"file\\\": file_path,\\n                \\\"status\\\": t.get(\\\"status\\\"),\\n                \\\"durationMs\\\": t.get(\\\"durationMs\\\"),\\n                \\\"error\\\": t.get(\\\"error\\\")\\n            }\\n    return data.get(\\\"summary\\\", {}), tests\\n\\ndef compare(net4_path, mssql_path, details_dir):\\n    s_net4, t_net4 = extract_tests(net4_path)\\n    s_mssql, t_mssql = extract_tests(mssql_path)\\n\\n    out_lines = []\\n    def log(msg=\\\"\\\"):\\n        print(msg)\\n        out_lines.append(msg)\\n\\n    log(\\\"================================================================================\\\")\\n    log(\\\"                       SCM E2E PARITY REPORT (NET4 vs NET10)                    \\\")\\n    log(\\\"================================================================================\\\")\\n    log(f\\\"NET4  (Origin STG4) : {net4_path}\\\")\\n    l\n<truncated 4684 bytes>","Description":"\"Script to compare NET4 and NET10 test reports and summarize parity\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-scm-web\\\\03_qa\\\\scripts\\\\compare-parity.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing compare-parity.py script\"","toolSummary":"\"Create compare-parity.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
