{"step_index":7045,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-09T03:18:47Z","thinking":"The user's statement indicates a successful API call from the STG4 environment, confirmed by observing the `output-sale-charities` result. The key insight is that the API is functioning, however, it returns no data, likely due to the specific search parameters: null `KeySearch`, a specific set of `StoreIDs`, a date range between 10/02/2026 and 10/09/2026. This suggests the issue is data availability given the input parameters within that specific environment and date range.\n\n\nThe STG10 environment reports a `NullReferenceException` at line 71, whereas STG4 returns a 204, indicating no data. The crucial difference appears to be the handling of the request object `Reqs` in the `Search` method within the STG10 environment. ASP.NET Core's binding mechanism for date parameters from the input string needs to be examined, especially how the `OutputSaleCharitySearchReq` class is defined and used.\n\n\nThe STG10 environment's culture setting within the Linux Docker container must be determined as it impacts date parsing. Given the `en-US` culture, dates are expected in `MM/DD/YYYY` format, and the client-side code reveals the application sends date strings in this expected format, so the date format is unlikely to be the root issue, but it is a factor to consider. The issue could be with how the dates are handled at the server during the model binding, despite correct formatting from the client-side date selections.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"dotnet test 02_target/tests/Unit/CoC.Web.SCM.Unit.Tests/CoC.Web.SCM.Unit.Tests.csproj --filter \\\"FullyQualifiedName~Model\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"E:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking test filter\"","toolSummary":"\"Run model tests\""}}]}
