{"step_index":7351,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-09T03:43:54Z","thinking":"The `NullReferenceException` stems from a null `Reqs` object. The `Reqs` object is null because form binding failed, and this failure is due to exceeding the system's key count limit. The form had 1380 `StoreIDs`, but the limit is only 1024. Therefore, when code tried to access a property on `Reqs`, it threw this exception.\n\n\nDouble-checking the fix against the documented bug-fix procedure, it appears the root cause has been addressed by increasing the system's form value count limit. The updated configuration was committed, tagged, and merged to the staging environments. Now reviewing the steps against `DEV_HANDBOOK.md` to ensure completion.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"git branch --show-current; git status --short\"","Cwd":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-scm-web\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking current branch and status\"","toolSummary":"\"Check final git branch and status\""}}]}
