{"step_index":7903,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-09T04:32:29Z","content":"Nguyên nhân khiến 2 URL trả ra kết quả khác nhau (STG4 hiển thị giao diện 403 chuẩn, còn STG10 bị **HTTP ERROR 500**) như sau:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Phân tích nguyên nhân gốc rễ (Root Cause)\n\n#### Trên STG4 (.NET Framework / MVC5):\n1. Khi truy cập `https://scm-stg4.concung.vn/Error/Unauthorized`, Controller [ErrorController.cs](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/01_origin/CoC.Web.SCM/Controllers/ErrorController.cs) kiểm tra nếu Session có đăng nhập (`Session[\"UserPricinpal\"] != null`) thì `return View();`.\n2. View [Unauthorized.cshtml](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/01_origin/CoC.Web.SCM/Views/Error/Unauthorized.cshtml) sử dụng Layout `_Layout.cshtml`.\n3. Trong `_Layout.cshtml`, MVC5 gọi `@Html.Action(\"LoadUserLogin\", \"Home\")` và `@Html.Action(\"Menu\", \"Home\")`.\n4. Trong kiến trúc cũ, `Session` và `User` được luân chuyển xuyên suốt trong cùng context nên thông tin user/quyền được nạp đầy đủ -> Render ra thanh menu màu hồng, avatar `G`, breadcrumb `Quản lý hàng hóa` và nội dung lỗi `Error 403 - Bạn không có quyền thao tác`.\n\n---\n\n#### Trên STG10 (.NET 10 / ASP.NET Core) — Chuỗi lỗi gây ra HTTP 500:\n1. **[ErrorController.cs](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/CoC.Web.SCM/Controllers/ErrorController.cs)** không gắn filter `[MvcAuthorize]` (điều này hoàn toàn bình thường vì trang báo lỗi không được chặn quyền).\n2. Tuy nhiên, trong mã nguồn migrate của SCM, việc gán `HttpContext.User = user;` **chỉ được thực hiện duy nhất bên trong `MvcAuthorizeAttribute.OnActionExecutionAsync`**. Vì `ErrorController` không có `[MvcAuthorize]`, filter này **không chạy**, dẫn đến `HttpContext.User` trên request `/Error/Unauthorized` là ClaimsPrincipal mặc định (chưa được gán `UserPrincipal`).\n3. `ErrorController.Unauthorized()` kiểm tra `UserSessionStore.Exists(HttpContext.Session)` thấy có session nên gọi `return View();`\n<truncated 2802 bytes>\nork/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/02_target/CoC.Web.Place/Controllers/HomeController.cs#L28-L33):\n  ```csharp\n  private UserPrincipal CurrentUser\n  {\n      get { return UserSessionStore.Load(HttpContext.Session); }\n  }\n  ```\n  Trực tiếp đọc từ `UserSessionStore.Load(HttpContext.Session)`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Giải pháp khắc phục triệt để\n\n1. **SCM Web - [Startup.cs](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/CoC.Web.SCM/Startup.cs)**: Thêm middleware ngay sau `app.UseSession();` để đồng bộ session principal vào `context.User` cho mọi request đã đăng nhập (kể cả các action không có `[MvcAuthorize]` như ErrorController, ChildAction, v.v.):\n   ```csharp\n   app.UseSession();\n   app.Use((context, next) =>\n   {\n       if (!(context.User is UserPrincipal) && UserSessionStore.Exists(context.Session))\n       {\n           var user = UserSessionStore.Load(context.Session);\n           if (user != null)\n           {\n               context.User = user;\n           }\n       }\n       return next();\n   });\n   ```\n2. **SCM Web - [HomeController.cs](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/CoC.Web.SCM/Controllers/HomeController.cs#L22-L25)**: Bổ sung fallback đọc session giống kiến trúc DC Web:\n   ```csharp\n   private UserPrincipal CurrentUser\n   {\n       get { return (User as UserPrincipal) ?? UserSessionStore.Load(HttpContext?.Session); }\n   }\n   ```\n3. **SCM Web - [ErrorController.cs](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/CoC.Web.SCM/Controllers/ErrorController.cs)**: Đảm bảo `Unauthorized()`, `Error()`, `NotFound()` nạp `HttpContext.User` trước khi `return View();`.\n4. **Đồng bộ bổ sung sang DC Web và Place Web** (theo rule của anh): Kiểm tra và bổ sung middleware này vào `Startup.cs` của DC và Place để đồng bộ kiến trúc .NET 10.\n\nAnh có muốn em tiến hành tạo branch fix, sửa code và thực hiện theo đúng quy trình Git/DEV_HANDBOOK cho SCM (và đồng bộ sang DC/Place) luôn không?","thinking":"The script for restoring the Bill of Materials is complete and functioning as expected. The user reports differing views from two URLs, one indicating an unauthorized access error and the other presenting an apparent error state.\n\n\nOn the STG4 environment, the unauthorized error page includes standard layout elements like the user profile and menu due to the presence of a valid session. STG10, utilizing ASP.NET Core, has explicitly excluded authorization filters for the error controller, suggesting a different approach to handling unauthorized access. The core difference appears to be how the `User` object is populated within the request lifecycle.\n\n\nThe `AuthorizeAttribute` configuration uses a cookie authentication stub, with the actual user session managed separately. This means the `HttpContext.User` in the unauthorized error flow won't be the expected `UserPrincipal`. The layout then tries to read session data to retrieve the `CurrentUser`. Consequently, `ControllerBase.User` within the `HomeController` is not castable to `UserPrincipal` and remains null.\n\n\nThe `NullReferenceException` stems from `CurrentUser` being null within the menu rendering, causing a cascade effect through the error handling mechanism. The global exception handler redirects to an error view that re-invokes the menu, repeating the null reference and leading to a fatal server error due to the secondary exception. Therefore, the fix requires making `CurrentUser` safe to access in the menu, particularly during error handling scenarios.\n\n\nThe difference in `CurrentUser` implementation across projects highlights the inconsistent handling of user sessions.  The `cci-dc-web` project's `CurrentUser` property safely handles cases where the `User` is not a `UserPrincipal`, but other projects do not.\n\nThe proposed solution focuses on `cci-scm-web` to address the unauthorized access issue. A middleware will be added to ensure the `HttpContext.User` is populated from the session, even for requests bypassing authorization filters, making session dat\n<truncated 1668 bytes>\necific reason for STG10's HTTP 500 error, not directly fixing it.\n\n\nSTG4 renders the full 403 error page because the user session is preserved, allowing access to layout elements that depend on user data. The `ErrorController` logic redirects to the home page if no session is found, otherwise, it renders the view. The layout reads the user's session data and renders the header.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe `ErrorController` in STG10 lacks authorization, so `MvcAuthorizeAttribute` doesn't execute, leaving `HttpContext.User` as the default principal.  Although the session exists and the layout attempts to load the user from it, the menu component is still invoked with a null or unauthenticated user. This results in the NullReferenceException within `HomeController.Menu` and ultimately leads to the HTTP 500 error.\n\n\nThe `NullReferenceException` stems from the `HomeController.Menu` method attempting to access `CurrentUser.IsPermission` when `CurrentUser` is null. This occurs because `HttpContext.User` is not populated with a `UserPrincipal` in the error handling path. The global exception handler redirects to an error view that re-invokes the menu through a layout, thus triggering a secondary exception. This results in ASP.NET Core terminating the response and producing an HTTP 500 error.\n\n\nProjects `cci-dc-web` and `cci-store-location-web` (Place) handle session-to-User population more robustly, avoiding the null reference. `cci-dc-web`'s `CurrentUser` property safely falls back to session data. `cci-store-location-web` (Place) directly loads the user from the session.\n\nFor `cci-scm-web`, the fix involves a middleware that ensures `HttpContext.User` is populated from the session, irrespective of authorization filters.  This middleware will be added after session use, guaranteeing user data availability even during error handling and in contexts bypassing authentication. The `CurrentUser` property and relevant error actions will be updated to consistently load `UserPrincipal` from the session.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content","thinking"]}
