{"step_index":8431,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:32:39Z","thinking":"Analyzing the failing tests, specifically the 128 regressions, to identify and categorize error clusters accurately is the immediate goal. The provided files, including the summary reports, will offer the necessary details on affected screens, error messages, and potential root causes. The goal is to establish the scope of remaining unresolved issues.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"node -e \\\"\\nconst fs = require('fs');\\nconst content = fs.readFileSync('03_qa/reports/details/parity-summary.txt', 'utf8');\\nconst lines = content.split('\\\\n');\\nconst regressions = [];\\nlet cur = null;\\nfor (const line of lines) {\\n  if (line.includes('[REGRESSION]')) {\\n    if (cur) regressions.push(cur);\\n    cur = { title: line.trim(), error: '', status: '' };\\n  } else if (cur) {\\n    if (line.includes('Status:')) cur.status = line.trim();\\n    if (line.includes('STG10 Error:')) cur.error = line.replace('STG10 Error:', '').trim();\\n  }\\n}\\nif (cur) regressions.push(cur);\\n\\nconst errorGroups = {};\\nregressions.forEach(r => {\\n  let cat = 'Other';\\n  const full = (r.status + ' ' + r.error).trim();\\n  if (r.status.includes('STG10=skipped')) {\\n    cat = 'STG10 Skipped (Do prerequisite/dependency/data bị skip trên stg10)';\\n  } else if (full.includes('timeout') || full.includes('timedOut')) {\\n    cat = 'Timeout (30s/90s/120s - API chậm, selector không xuất hiện hoặc spinner treo)';\\n  } else if (full.includes('expect(received).not.toBeNull()') || full.includes('toBeVisible') || full.includes('toBeEnabled')) {\\n    cat = 'Assertion UI/Selector (Dữ liệu trả về rỗng hoặc element ID/Class khác biệt)';\\n  } else if (full.includes('500') || full.includes('Internal Server Error')) {\\n    cat = 'HTTP 500 Backend/API Error';\\n  }\\n  if (!errorGroups[cat]) errorGroups[cat] = [];\\n  errorGroups[cat].push(r);\\n});\\n\\nfor (const [cat, items] of Object.entries(errorGroups)) {\\n  console.log(`\\\\n=== ${cat} (${items.length} tests) ===`);\\n  const screens = new Set(items.map(x => x.title.split('|')[0].replace('[REGRESSION]', '').trim()));\\n  console.log('Screens affected (' + screens.size + '):', Array.from(screens).slice(0, 15).join(', ') + (screens.size > 15 ? '...' : ''));\\n  console.log('Sample tests:');\\n  items.slice(0, 3).forEach(x => console.log('  -', x.title, '=>', x.status, x.error ? '| ' + x.error : ''));\\n}\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-scm-web\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Analyzing SCM regression error groups\"","toolSummary":"\"Analyze SCM regression groups\""}}]}
