EB activities for the standup report. The user's provided template is being used to structure the report. Need to populate the \"Yesterday\" section with the user's provided context on SCM WEB work.\n\n\n\nYesterday (Oct 12), SCM WEB activities included resolving a startup crash related to user permissions, verifying successful builds and API responses after PR merges, and executing a full E2E regression test suite on STG10, resulting in 2357 passes and automated dashboard reporting. Also, a deep parity analysis between STG4 (Oracle) and STG1 was performed.\n\nToday's SCM WEB plan involves verifying staging10 after PR merges, focusing on config/code consistency, and addressing regressions identified in 128 E2E test cases, re-running the tests, and updating the dashboard.\n\n\nYesterday, the team isolated 39 real Parity Fail cases across 32 screens, after eliminating 514 environmental errors; these were grouped into categories (Backend/DTO/Validation; 403 Permissions; UI/Format/Redirect). Detailed investigation of the `BonusOutputSales/Search` API 500 error started, comparing Protobuf (STG4) versus JSON (STG10) mechanisms, hypothesizing validation, DateTime format or permission discrepancies as the cause.\n\nToday, the team will debug and fix the `BonusOutputSales/Search` API 500 error, focusing on DateTime format and payload validation. Addressing the 39 Parity Fail cases will begin, prioritizing Backend/DTO/Validation and 403 Permission issues. Following fixes, verification testing and E2E/Dashboard updates will be completed.\n\n\n"}
