{"step_index":9096,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:04:09Z","thinking":"If the token was empty, other APIs should not be callable, implying a potential bypass or caching issue. Suspect that some other mechanism, like a default credential or a session cookie, might be handling the authentication, even when the token is missing. The observed behavior suggests that the token's absence doesn't always strictly enforce access control.\n\n\nThe failure of `BonusOutputSales/Search` specifically points to a difference in its dependency injection chain. The `ApiHelper`, injected through multiple layers, appears to perform initialization in its constructor that includes reading the authorization header from the current HTTP context. If this header is missing or malformed, the API will fail.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":"true","MatchPerLine":"true","Query":"\"IApiHelper\"","SearchPath":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-scm-api\\\\01_origin\\\\Coc.API.SCM\\\\Controllers\"","toolAction":"\"Checking which controllers inject IApiHelper\"","toolSummary":"\"Search IApiHelper in controllers\""}}]}
