{"step_index":9220,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:35:30Z","thinking":"When a 500 error occurs, the content type must be checked. If it is plain text, the raw content is the error message. Otherwise, attempt to deserialize the content into an error response object. If successful and the error message exists, assign the error message. Otherwise, use the response object to get the error message.\n\n\nThe code checks for an API 500 error and extracts the error message. It prioritizes the raw content if the response is plain text. Otherwise, it attempts deserialization to get a structured error message. If deserialization fails, it resorts to logging the raw API response body as the error. Crucially, the caught exception is re-thrown with a custom message that captures the relevant context and the raw API body details. This detailed error message, logged by the controller, is then stored to the logging system. The error details from `_CodeStep.ErrorMessage` are available to external logging, although not visible to the user locally.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-scm-web\\\\02_target\\\\CoC.Web.SCM\\\\Helpers\\\\ApiHelper.cs\"","EndLine":"620","StartLine":"580","toolAction":"\"Viewing getRawContent in ApiHelper.cs\"","toolSummary":"\"View getRawContent\""}}]}
