{"step_index":9799,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:56:59Z","thinking":"The `FileCount` method appears to be the source of an `InvalidDataException`, likely because it's accessing `request.Form` when the request's content type isn't a form. This suggests the code is attempting to treat a raw-body upload as a form submission, leading to the exception. The conditional check `request.HasFormContentType` should prevent this, so there is likely a situation where the check is bypassed or incorrect.\n\n\nIt appears the exception \"Missing content-type boundary\" stems from an issue within `FormFeature.GetBoundary()`, called during `request.Form` access. The code relies on the `HasFormContentType` check, evaluating whether the `ContentType` is \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" or \"multipart/form-data\". However, `FormFeature.ReadForm()` still requires a valid boundary within the `multipart/form-data` content, even if the content type check passes. A missing boundary causes this specific exception.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"e:\\\\Work\\\\Place_Migrate\\\\cci-scm-web\\\\02_target\\\\CoC.Web.SCM\\\\Controllers\\\\DirectivesController.cs\"","EndLine":"3295","StartLine":"3275","toolAction":"\"Viewing ReadBody in DirectivesController\"","toolSummary":"\"View ReadBody in DirectivesController\""}}]}
