{"step_index":9847,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:02:30Z","content":"Nguyên nhân gây ra lỗi **`System.IO.InvalidDataException: Missing content-type boundary`** khi import Excel tại `CategoryAttributeMonths` được xác định chi tiết như sau:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Nguyên nhân gốc (Root Cause)\n\nLỗi xảy ra do sự khác biệt cơ chế xử lý Form giữa **ASP.NET MVC 5 (.NET 4.8)** và **ASP.NET Core (.NET 10)** kết hợp với cách frontend AngularJS gửi request upload:\n\n#### Phía Frontend (`FileUpload.js`):\nKhi bạn bấm chọn file Excel ở popup import (chế độ single file `!scope.root.IsMultipleFile`), directive [FileUpload.js:L235-L243](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/CoC.Web.SCM/wwwroot/script-handler/app/directives/FileUpload/FileUpload.js#L235-L243) thực hiện:\n```javascript\nobjFileNew.Http.open(\"POST\", scope.root.ActionUpload, true);\nobjFileNew.Http.setRequestHeader(\"Content-Type\", \"multipart/form-data\");\nobjFileNew.Http.setRequestHeader(\"FileName\", UtilJS.String.RemoveUnicode(strName));\n...\nobjFileNew.Http.send(objFileNew.FileInput); // Gửi raw Binary Blob, KHÔNG dùng FormData\n```\n* Frontend gửi **raw binary stream** trực tiếp vào body (chứ không đóng gói `FormData`).\n* Nhưng header lại bị gán cứng là `Content-Type: multipart/form-data` **mà KHÔNG có tham số `boundary`** (thông thường khi dùng `FormData` thì browser mới tự sinh chuỗi `boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary...`).\n\n#### Phía Backend (`DirectivesController.cs`):\nTại [DirectivesController.cs:L3297-L3300](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/CoC.Web.SCM/Controllers/DirectivesController.cs#L3297-L3300):\n```csharp\nprivate static int FileCount(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpRequest request)\n{\n    return request.HasFormContentType ? request.Form.Files.Count : 0;\n}\n```\n\n* **Trên .NET 4.8 (Origin):** Thuộc tính `Request.Files` của IIS/System.Web nếu gặp request không có boundary thì chỉ trả về collection rỗng `Count = 0` chứ **không throw Exception**. Code chạy tiếp xuống nhánh `else if (fileContents.Length > 0)` đọc byte từ body và lưu file bình thường.\n* **Trên .NET 10 (Target ASP.NET Core):**\n  1. `request.HasFormContentType` kiểm tra header: thấy có chữ `multipart/form-data` $\\rightarrow$ trả về **`true`**.\n  2. Code truy cập vào `request.Form.Files.Count`.\n  3. Kestrel / ASP.NET Core gọi `FormFeature.ReadForm()` $\\rightarrow$ parse header tìm `boundary`.\n  4. Vì header không có `boundary`, ASP.NET Core quăng ngay exception:\n     ```text\n     System.IO.InvalidDataException: Missing content-type boundary.\n        at Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.Features.FormFeature.GetBoundary(...)\n     ```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Cách xử lý (Fix)\n\nBản thân hàm [saveFile(...)](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/02_target/CoC.Web.SCM/Controllers/DirectivesController.cs#L1190-L1204) trong backend **đã có sẵn** logic lưu file từ raw stream `fileContents` và header `FileName`. Nó chỉ bị crash sớm tại hàm `FileCount` khi cố gắng đọc `request.Form`.\n\nChỉ cần bọc `try-catch` an toàn trong hàm `FileCount` để tái hiện đúng hành vi của .NET Framework cũ (nếu Form không parse được do thiếu boundary thì coi như `FileCount = 0` và để nhánh raw body `fileContents` xử lý):\n\n```csharp\nprivate static int FileCount(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpRequest request)\n{\n    try\n    {\n        return request.HasFormContentType ? request.Form.Files.Count : 0;\n    }\n    catch\n    {\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n> **Ghi chú thêm:** Hàm `FileCount` tương tự ở cả **DC Web** ([DirectivesController.cs:L901](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-dc-web/02_target/CoC.Web.DC/Controllers/DirectivesController.cs#L901)) và **Place Web** ([DirectivesController.cs:L458](file:///e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-store-location-web/02_target/CoC.Web.Place/Controllers/DirectivesController.cs#L458)) cũng đang dùng chung pattern này. Nếu cần, ta sẽ apply fix này đồng bộ cho cả 3 repo.","thinking":"The error \"Missing content-type boundary\" strongly suggests the server is receiving malformed form data during the Excel import. The `FormFeature` class in the ASP.NET Core framework handles incoming form data, and the exception indicates a problem with the expected structure of the multipart/form-data request, specifically the absence of the boundary delimiter. A likely hypothesis is that either the client is not correctly constructing the HTTP request, or the server-side configuration for processing the Excel file import has a misconfiguration of the expected `Content-Type`.\n\n\nAnalyzing the stack trace reveals the error occurs within the `FormFeature` class during form data reading, specifically during the asynchronous form reading operation. This reinforces the initial suspicion of malformed or incomplete form data. The traceback indicates the issue arises within the `UploadFileAPI` function and subsequent controller methods, pointing to the Excel file upload process.\n\n\nThe frontend's use of \"multipart/form-data\" without a boundary in a raw binary upload likely causes the issue. The .NET Framework version gracefully handled this incorrect content type by falling back to reading the input stream directly, whereas the .NET 10 target with ASP.NET Core likely expects the multipart structure to be valid. This difference explains the behavior discrepancy between the environments.\n\n\nThe code explicitly checks for form content type and attempts to read form files, but the missing boundary causes an exception. The server-side code actually *already* includes fallback logic to handle raw binary uploads, which could have been used if the `FileCount` check hadn't failed. The root issue is an unnecessary `Form` data attempt when raw binary upload is intended. This triggers the boundary parsing, which is absent in the `Content-Type`.\n\n\nThe `FileCount` method in `DirectivesController.cs` attempts to parse form data, but catches exceptions on malformed requests, returning zero. This causes a bypass of the intended form-data handling, allowing raw binary uploads to be processed as though they were valid uploads by checking the headers directly. The same vulnerability exists in both the DC Web and Place Web applications. The catch-all exception handling masks the problem.\n\n\n"}
