{"step_index":12119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-14T06:05:33Z","thinking":"The `searchButton()` is defined by the CSS selectors `a.btn.cc-btn-color-violet, button.cc-btn-color-violet`. Examining the HTML, specifically line 53 of a relevant file, reveals a button element that matches this pattern. The `ng-show` directive, controlled by the `Permisstion.Read` variable, conditionally applies the `ng-hide` class, effectively hiding the button when the permission is not granted (resulting in `display: none !important`).\n\n\nThe `.filter({ visible: true })` in the locator definition causes `searchButton().count()` to return 0 when the button is hidden, which leads to `click()` throwing an error and waiting 30 seconds. To avoid this, a guard is required to check `searchButton().count()` before clicking. The approach used in another test case, specifically checking the count and skipping the test if the button is hidden, seems appropriate.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"e:/Work/Place_Migrate/cci-scm-web/03_qa/e2e/confirm-gs-ms/confirm-gs-ms.e2e.spec.ts\"","EndLine":"70","StartLine":"40","toolAction":"\"Viewing lines 40-70 of confirm-gs-ms spec\"","toolSummary":"\"View confirm-gs-ms lines 40-70\""}}]}
